 ## Languages

 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server chooses the supported language with the
+highest positive q-value in the request's `Accept-Language` header (default
+q-value `1`; ties use header order). Region tags such as `ko-KR` and `en-US`
+select their base language. Unsupported languages and q-value `0` entries
+are ignored. If no supported language is acceptable, or the header is absent,
+the server uses `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`). Every error code has a Korean
+and English message, including unexpected server errors.
